  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Web App**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core functionality: designing a web app (\"scoreboard\") tailored for \"Mixed Reality Shooter\". My aim is to efficiently parse and display data from JSON files generated post-match, presenting the results in a clear leaderboard format for the user to view.\n\n\n**Outlining Key Features**\n\nI\'ve outlined the critical features, like viewing daily results and navigating dates, along with individual player stats focusing on team scores. I\'m also planning for a print-friendly layout with match selection and a file upload mechanism. I\'ll be using Next.js, React, and Tailwind CSS. Now, I\'m focusing on defining the TypeScript interfaces for the JSON data to get the data format set. Next up, is a local state (using `localStorage` for now, no backend) to persist match data.\n\n\n**Developing Component Designs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the key UI components. I plan to use `lucide-react` for icons, and have installed `date-fns` for potential date manipulation, though native JavaScript dates might suffice. I\'ll stick with raw Tailwind CSS to build custom components. I\'ve broken down the development plan into clear steps: setting up dependencies, defining TypeScript types for `MatchData` and `PlayerStat`, and creating a `useMatchData` hook for `localStorage` state management. Next I\'ll start building the components, and a `Header`, `UploadSection`, `MatchList`, and `MatchCard`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 420850981
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
